      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/17/pope-leo-discharged-from-hospital-after-cancer-operation",
      "description": "<p>Doctors say pontiff is ‘fit for discharge’ after operation to remove cancerous tumour from his lung</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/16/pope-leo-lung-cancer-surgery-lobectomy\">Pope Leo lung cancer surgery: what kind of operation did he have and what happens next?</a></p></li></ul><p>Pope Leo has been discharged from hospital in Rome after <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/13/pope-leo-hospital-operation-growth-lung\">undergoing an operation to remove a cancerous tumour from his lung</a>.</p><p>Leo, 71, was deemed “fit for discharge”, his doctors, Luigi Carbone and Stefano Margaritora, said in a statement published by the Vatican.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/17/pope-leo-discharged-from-hospital-after-cancer-operation\">Continue reading...</a>",
